    "id": "q2",
    "text": "Is the refused-command check for write to a read-only register ordered after the register-number range check?",
    "default": "Yes, register >= 8 gives result 3 and only 0..7 can give result 5.",
    "reason": "The request does not state precedence.",
    "answer": "Yes. The spec gives code 3 for any register number above 7 and assigns code 5 only to writes to registers 0 and 4..7, so code 5 can never apply to register 8 or higher. The two checks do not overlap, and the stated order is the range check first, then the read-only check.",
